   in Section 2(b) are not Copyright and Similar Rights.

d. Effective Technological Measures means those measures that, in the
   absence of proper authority, may not be circumvented with informational
   and technical means, or those rights holders may use to prevent
   infringements of their rights under the Copyright and Similar Rights
   held by the Licensor.

e. Exceptions and Limitations means fair use, fair dealing, and/or
   any other exception or limitation to Copyright and Similar Rights
   that reduces or eliminates the need to obtain permission under the
   Copyright and Similar Rights held by the Licensor.

f. Licensed Material means the artistic or literary work, database, or
   other material to which the Licensor applied the Public License.

g. Licensed Rights means the rights granted to You subject to the
   terms and conditions of this Public License, which are limited to all
   Copyright and Similar Rights that, as exercised by You, are capable of
   being further shared with others pursuant to the terms and conditions
   of this Public License.

h. Licensor means the individual(s) or entity(ies) granting rights under
   this Public License.

i. NonCommercial means not primarily intended for or directed towards
   commercial advantage or monetary compensation. For purposes of this
   Public License, the exchange of money or other forms of compensation
   are not

j. Share means to provide material to another person by any means or
   format that enables another person to access, view, listen to, or
   otherwise experience the material.

k. Sui Generis Database Rights means rights other than copyright
   resulting from Directive 96/9/EC of the European Parliament and of
